error: dict keys 1 and "1" both render as mapping key '1'
 = a mapping holds each key once: a dict renders a string key as its text and a number key as its rendered text, so keys such as "x" and :x, or 1 and "1", collide; render 'dict.to-list(d)' to output [key, value] pairs instead
